            0.12,
            0.719,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "India has a rich history of measurement systems dating back to ancient times. Angula (finger width), multiples of angula, dhanusa, and yojana are some of the units mentioned in ancient Indian literature, and used in measuring artefacts, architecture, and"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.259,
            0.27,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "",
